[tool_result] toolu_01GsjxiLR3tm7csrSjmcuCsm 1	# Phase 1 decision memo — local MVP cue trainer
2	
3	## Goal
4	Ship a fullscreen, low-latency go/no-go reaction trainer the athlete can use in
5	his gym within two weeks of his next competition. Single drill type, single
6	input (Space bar), local persistence, immediate per-rep feedback, session
7	summary on stop.
8	
9	## Non-goals (Phase 1)
10	- Drill configuration UI (Phase 2)
11	- Video opponent clips (Phase 3)
12	- Configurable input mappings / kiosk polish (Phase 4)
13	- Pose detection (Phase 5)
14	- Long-term analytics dashboards (Phase 6)
15	
16	## Key decisions
17	
18	### D1. Response model: single commit key
19	Phase 1 uses one input — **Space = commit**. Response *type* selection
20	(blitz vs jam vs counter, etc.) is a Phase 2+ concern. This keeps the
21	perception-action loop pure (see / commit / measure) and matches the spec's
22	"discourage half-commitments" principle without forcing a key-choice subtask
23	that itself adds cognitive delay.
24	
25	A foot pedal in Phase 4
