[text] Review the Phase 2 changes in this repo for code quality, architecture compliance, test sufficiency, and maintainability per `/home/aaron/dev/projects/aaron/pointfight-reactor/docs/QUALITY_GATES.md`.

Phase context: Phase 1 shipped a local go/no-go reaction trainer; Phase 2 adds round structure, configurable input, motion indicator, longer pre-cue delay, and an optional penalty counter. Phone-as-sensor was descoped to a new Phase 2b (see `artifacts/phase-update.json` and `artifacts/decision-memo.md`).

Scope of review:
- `app/src/engine/types.ts` (new DrillConfig fields, optional SessionRecord fields, RepRecord roundIndex + inputSource, validation constants)
- `app/src/engine/drill.ts` (new pure helpers `validateDrillConfig`, `pendingPenalties`)
- `app/src/engine/drill.test.ts` (new tests appended to existing file)
- `app/src/store/session.ts` (full rewrite — round transition logic, persistSession refactor, clearPenalty/nextRound actions, inputSource stamping)
- `app/src/store/session.test.ts` (4 new tests for round transitions, penalty counter, inputSource stamping)
- `app/src/store/db.ts` (Dexie schema bumped to version(2), settings store added)
- `app/src/store/settings.ts`, `app/src/store/settings-types.ts`, `app/src/store/settings.test.ts` (new module)
- `app/src/ui/SettingsScreen.tsx` (new), `app/src/ui/RestScreen.tsx` (new), `app/src/ui/TrainerScreen.tsx` (extended), `app/src/ui/IdleScreen.tsx` (extended), `app/src/ui/SummaryScreen.tsx` (extended)
- `app/src/App.tsx` (settings route)
- `app/src/App.css` (new motion-pulse, rest, settings styles)
- `docs/PHASES.md` (Phase 2 scope split note + new Phase 2b)
- `artifacts/decision-memo.md`, `artifacts/phase-update.json`

What's already verified locally:
- `npm run lint` clean
- `npm run typecheck` clean
- `npm test` — 47/47 pass (was 28 in Phase 1)
- `npm run build` succeeds

Specifically check for:
- DRY: any rep-record or session-record construction duplicated across paths?
- Drift: any place where round-end logic could be off by one (final round, maxReps boundary, work-time-expiry-mid-feedback)?
- Test sufficiency: do the new tests cover the primary path of each new behavior, and at least one edge case for each?
- Architecture: is settings persistence properly isolated from the Zustand store? Are the engine helpers pure?
- Correctness risks specific to this stack: useEffect timer cleanup, hooks order across the new SettingsScreen rebind flow, Dexie v1→v2 migration safety for users with Phase 1 sessions in their browser.

Report verdict: APPROVE / REQUEST_CHANGES with specific findings keyed by file:line. Keep it under 400 words.
